# 9. AUTOMATED SEO AUDIT TOOL

Create an interactive SEO assessment tool.

Route: /free-seo-audit/

This should be a major lead-generation feature.

### User interface

Display a clean form with:

- Website URL.
- Work email.
- Optional name.
- Optional company name.
- Optional target market.
- Consent checkbox where required.

Primary CTA: "Analyze My Website"

Make it clear what information is collected and how it will be used.

### User flow

1. Visitor enters a website URL.
2. Validate the URL.
3. Validate the email address.
4. Explain the analysis scope.
5. Submit the request.
6. Process the URL securely on the server.
7. Display the results when analysis completes.
8. Offer an option to request a detailed consultation.

Avoid forcing visitors to provide unnecessary personal information before they can understand the tool's value.

### Initial audit checks

Where technically possible, assess:

- HTTP response status.
- HTTPS availability.
- Page title presence and length.
- Meta description presence and length.
- H1 presence.
- Canonical tag.
- Robots directives.
- Robots.txt availability.
- XML sitemap discovery.
- Basic internal-link counts.
- Image alt-text coverage.
- HTML language declaration.
- Viewport configuration.
- Redirect behavior.
- Basic page size.
- Response time.
- Structured-data presence.
- Obvious duplicate title or heading issues on the analyzed page.

Optional checks may include mobile performance and Core Web Vitals when supported by a configured performance API.

Clearly distinguish direct observations from estimates.

Do not claim to have analyzed the entire website if only one page was checked.

### Results page

Display:

- Overall assessment.
- Passed checks.
- Warnings.
- Failed checks.
- Individual explanations.
- Recommended next actions.
- Limitations of the assessment.
- Consultation CTA.

If using a score, document how it is calculated.

Do not imply that the score is a Google ranking score or an official Google metric.

### Report generation

Generate a branded, printable report with:

- Website URL.
- Assessment timestamp.
- Checks performed.
- Findings.
- Prioritized recommendations.
- Relevant limitations.
- Consultation CTA.

If PDF generation is implemented, generate the report on the server using a suitable library.

### Security requirements

The audit tool accepts user-controlled URLs and therefore requires strict protections against server-side request forgery and abuse.

Implement:

- HTTP and HTTPS URL validation.
- Blocking of loopback and private network addresses.
- Blocking of link-local and cloud metadata addresses.
- DNS resolution checks.
- Validation of every resolved IP address.
- Protection against DNS rebinding.
- Redirect limits and destination revalidation.
- Request timeouts.
- Response-size limits.
- Safe content-type handling.
- Rate limiting.
- Abuse monitoring.
- Request quotas.
- Safe error messages.

Do not fetch arbitrary user-supplied URLs without these protections.

Do not execute JavaScript from analyzed websites.

Do not collect or store unnecessary website content.

### Performance and cost controls

Use background jobs if analysis takes more than a few seconds.

Provide progress indicators, timeouts, retries where appropriate, and clear failure states.

Cache suitable results to reduce duplicate requests and API costs.

Use external APIs only when configured and document their limitations.

