# 15. PERFORMANCE AND CORE WEB VITALS

Performance is a major selling point for this project.

Build the site with a performance-first approach.

### Targets

Aim for the following Core Web Vitals thresholds at the 75th percentile of real-user measurements:

- Largest Contentful Paint (LCP): 2.5 seconds or less.
- Interaction to Next Paint (INP): 200 milliseconds or less.
- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS): 0.1 or less.

Aim for a Lighthouse performance score of 90 or higher on representative pages, where practical.

These are targets to verify, not guaranteed results.

### Implementation requirements

- Minimize unnecessary JavaScript.
- Use code splitting.
- Lazy-load below-the-fold images.
- Avoid lazy-loading the primary LCP image.
- Use responsive images.
- Prefer modern image formats.
- Set image dimensions to prevent layout shifts.
- Optimize font loading.
- Remove unused CSS.
- Avoid excessive third-party scripts.
- Cache static assets appropriately.
- Compress responses.
- Use efficient server rendering or static generation.
- Keep animations lightweight.
- Avoid large, unnecessary video backgrounds.
- Load analytics scripts responsibly.
- Avoid blocking the main thread with expensive tasks.

Use a CDN when appropriate.

Test the homepage, service pages, blog, audit tool, and contact page.

Document performance bottlenecks and the measurements used to evaluate them.

Do not report Lighthouse scores or Core Web Vitals measurements as verified until tests have been run.

